  "description_blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The N20 Reduction Gear Motor is a low-power reduction motor with a D-shaped output shaft, suitable for applications requiring continuous rotation of objects. The motor can be connected to the Power Distribution Board (PDB) with 4 Channels using the Wire Pair with SH1.0-2PIN-5CM/10CM/20CM."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Considerations"
    },
    {
      "kind": "bullet",
      "text": "Please use a power supply within the working voltage range."
    },
    {
      "kind": "bullet",
      "text": "Avoid immersing the motor in water or getting the motor wet."
    },
    {
      "kind": "bullet",
      "text": "Use screws of the appropriate length to secure the gearbox to prevent thread slippage or damage to the gearbox from screws touching the gears."
    },
    {
      "kind": "bullet",
      "text": "When using glue/adhesive to fix the motor, to prevent damage, do not let the glue/adhesive seep into the gearbox, shaft, or motor interior."
    },
    {
      "kind": "bullet",
      "text": "Regularly add a small amount of lubricant/grease to the gearbox to improve its lifespan and reduce noise."
    }
  ],
